    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "Is the Scapia Credit Card lifetime free?",
        "answer": "Yes. The Scapia Credit Card is lifetime free, with no joining or annual fees. It is available through Federal Bank, BOBCARD and Axis Bank."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which banks issue the Scapia Credit Card?",
        "answer": "Scapia has partnered with Federal Bank, BOBCARD and Axis Bank. The cards are available on Visa, Mastercard and RuPay networks, depending on the issuing bank and card variant."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does the Scapia Credit Card have zero forex markup?",
        "answer": "Yes. Scapia offers 0% forex markup on international transactions. The applicable Visa or Mastercard exchange rate is used for currency conversion. Always choose the local currency instead of INR when paying abroad to avoid Dynamic Currency Conversion (DCC) charges."
      },
      {
        "question": "How much reward does the Scapia Credit Card offer?",
        "answer": "Eligible Visa and Mastercard transactions earn 10 Scapia Coins per ₹100 spent, equivalent to 2% value back. Eligible RuPay transactions earn 5 Coins per ₹100, equivalent to 1%. Travel bookings through the Scapia app can earn up to 4% value back. Reward rates and exclusions depend on the card variant."
      },
      {
        "question": "How can I redeem Scapia Coins?",
        "answer": "Scapia Coins can be redeemed for flights, hotels, trains, buses, experiences and shopping on the Scapia Store. Every 5 Scapia Coins are worth ₹1, and Coins are valid for 36 months. They cannot be converted into statement credit or transferred to airline and hotel loyalty programmes."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I get airport lounge access with Scapia?",
        "answer": "You need to spend ₹20,000 in the previous billing cycle to unlock Airport Privileges. Eligible cardholders can enjoy unlimited complimentary domestic lounge access or choose other airport benefits. Airport Privileges must be activated through the Scapia app before use."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use Scapia Airport Privileges for dining and shopping?",
        "answer": "Yes. Instead of visiting an airport lounge, you can use Airport Privileges for dining, shopping or spa services at participating airports. You can get up to ₹1,000 back in Scapia Coins on eligible spending, subject to the airport, outlet and card terms."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does Scapia offer international airport lounge access?",
        "answer": "No. Scapia does not currently offer complimentary international lounge access as a standard benefit. However, eligible international flight bookings of ₹50,000 or more through the Scapia app can unlock up to ₹2,000 back in rewards on dining or shopping at international terminals in India."
      },
      {
        "question": "Does Scapia offer rewards on utility and insurance payments?",
        "answer": "Reward exclusions depend on the issuing bank. Utility, telecom and insurance transactions are excluded from rewards on the Federal Bank variant under its revised terms. Check the latest reward terms for your Scapia card before making these payments."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use the Scapia RuPay Credit Card for UPI payments?",
        "answer": "Yes. Eligible Scapia RuPay credit cards support UPI payments to merchants. You can earn Scapia Coins on eligible transactions of ₹500 or more, subject to reward exclusions."
      }
    ],
